.TH PROSELIGN 1 "October 2026" "proselign" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proselign \- learn a writer's prose style and align text to it, locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proselign
.RB [ \-\-voice
.IR NAME ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B proselign train \-\-voice
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-append ]
.RB [ \-\-min\-words
.IR N ]
.IR PATH ...
.br
.B proselign tune \-\-voice
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-base
.IR HF_MODEL ]
.RB [ \-\-pairs\-only ]
.br
.B proselign voices
.br
.B proselign inspect
.I NAME
.br
.B proselign export
.I NAME
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-include\-sources ]
.br
.B proselign import
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B proselign delete
.I NAME
.br
.B proselign eval \-\-voice
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-samples
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proselign
is a filter. It reads text from standard input (or the named files), rewrites
it in the style of a previously learned
.IR voice ,
and writes the result to standard output. Standard output carries the
rewritten text and nothing else; all diagnostics go to standard error.
.PP
Facts, numbers, names, URLs, citations, quotations, code and Markdown
structure are preserved. Fenced code blocks, tables, HTML blocks, front
matter, e-mail headers and plain-text headings are copied verbatim and never
sent to the model. Numbers, document identifiers (such as Bates numbers),
quotations, URLs, e-mail addresses and list labels are sent as placeholders
and put back afterwards. Each rewritten chunk is checked: every protected
token, name and acronym must survive, as must every negation and modal verb
(not, never, may, will, could), every sentence (none dropped or invented),
and who is speaking and addressed; its length must stay close to the
original's. A failed chunk is retried once with feedback.
.PP
Then each rewrite is reviewed sentence by sentence. Only sentences that need
work are changed: one that breaks a style rule, runs far longer than the
author's sentences, or spells out what the author contracts. The model is
told which ones, and every other sentence is left exactly as written. A
changed sentence must keep its protected tokens, names, negations, modal
verbs and persons and add no name, and then a second model is asked only
whether the two say the same thing. A sentence that fails any of this gets
the original back (or, with
.BR \-\-strict ,
the command fails). Dropped sentences are restored and added ones removed;
list markers, the case of a sentence's first word and the whitespace between
sentences always come from the original. These checks are strong but not
perfect: read the changes before sending anything that matters.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B train
Measure the documents under each
.I PATH
and store the resulting voice: plain text and Markdown
.RB ( .txt ", " .md ),
Word
.RB ( .docx ,
and
.B .doc
from Word 6 through 2003),
.B .pdf
and
.B .mbox
mailboxes.
Text is extracted without running any other program. A mailbox should hold
mail you sent: each message counts as a document, and quoted replies,
forwarded messages, signatures and attachments are left out. Hidden files and
directories are skipped; a file that cannot be read (damaged, encrypted,
or a scanned PDF with no text) is skipped with a warning.
.B \-\-append
re-learns an existing voice from its previous sources plus the new ones.
.BI \-\-min\-words " N"
leaves out documents (and mailbox messages) shorter than
.I N
words, so the voice is learned from considered writing rather than quick
notes; an appended voice keeps its threshold.
Besides the measurements, training keeps the author's vocabulary habits
(preferred words, words never used, frequent sentence openers, serial comma,
spelling) and up to 200 typical passages, which are shown to the model as
examples. The passages stay in the local voice store and are left out of
exports.
.TP
.B eval
Measure how closely rewrites reproduce a voice: sample passages are
flattened into neutral prose by the model and rewritten back in the voice
(without themselves among the examples), and a stylometric distance is
reported for each version, with the share of the gap the rewrite closed.
Accepts the rewrite options, so models and settings can be compared.
Settings that depart from the author's habits on purpose
.RB ( passive_voice " = off, " first_person " other than " voice )
are set aside for the measurement, and the report names them.
The neutral versions are kept in the voice's directory (never exported) and
reused by later runs, so different models and settings are measured from the
same starting texts;
.B \-\-fresh
writes new ones with the current model.
Because any rewrite changes wording, the neutral texts are also rewritten
with no voice as a control, and the report says how much closer the voiced
rewrite came to the author than the control did;
.B \-\-no\-control
skips it (about a third faster).
.B \-\-repeats
.I N
(1\-10) rewrites every passage N times and reports the average with its
range across the runs, to tell a real difference from noise.
A second table splits each distance into what function words, sentence
length, word length and contractions contribute.
.B \-\-ablate
rewrites every passage again once for each part of the voice, with that
part left out (sentence length, contractions, person, passive voice, word
length, punctuation, vocabulary, tone, the example passages, the steering
feedback), and reports whether each part helps or hurts; use it with
.B \-\-repeats
2 or more.
.B \-\-samples
sets the number of passages (default 8);
.B \-\-json
prints the result as JSON.
.TP
.B tune
Fine-tune a model on a voice, so rewrites come from a model that has
learned the author's writing rather than one told about it. Passages of the
voice's source documents are flattened into neutral prose by the current
.BR \-\-model ,
giving pairs of neutral and original text (with facts masked as
placeholders on both sides); these are kept with the voice and reused. A
LoRA adapter is then trained on them (QLoRA, the base in 4-bit), converted
to GGUF and registered with Ollama as
.BI proselign\- NAME
on top of the same base model. Rewrites and
.B eval
in that voice then use the tuned model with a short prompt, unless
.B \-\-model
or
.B \-\-no\-tuned
is given;
.B eval
of a tuned voice uses only the 20 passages held out of training.
Training needs a CUDA GPU (16 GB is enough for a 14B model) and the
training extras
.RB ( "pip install 'proselign[tune]'" ).
.B \-\-base
names the Hugging Face weights behind
.B \-\-model
(default Qwen/Qwen2.5\-14B\-Instruct);
.BR \-\-epochs " (default 2), " \-\-rank " (default 16) and " \-\-name
adjust the training;
.B \-\-pairs\-only
writes the pairs and stops.
.TP
.B voices
List stored voices, one per line: identifier, display name, document count,
separated by tabs.
.TP
.B inspect
Print a voice's profile as JSON.
.TP
.B export
Write a voice to a portable
.B .proselign
archive. Corpus file paths and hashes are omitted unless
.B \-\-include\-sources
is given.
.TP
.B import
Install a voice from an archive. Archives are validated; nothing in them is
executed.
.TP
.B delete
Permanently remove a voice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-strength " N"
Degree of stylistic change from 0.0 (minimal) to 1.0 (full). Default 0.5.
.TP
.B \-\-format markdown\fR|\fBtext
How to segment input. Default markdown.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit with status 4 instead of keeping original text when a chunk fails
fidelity checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " openai-compat" \fR|\fB mock
Inference backend.
.B mock
echoes its input and is useful for testing pipelines.
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " URL"
Base URL of an OpenAI-compatible server. Default http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name to request.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Refuse any endpoint that is not a loopback address.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Sampling seed, for reproducible runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-examples " N"
Passages of the voice's own writing shown to the model per chunk, 0 to 8.
Default 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-candidates " N"
Rewrites generated per chunk, 1 to 5; the one stylometrically closest to
the voice is kept. Default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-chunk\-tokens " N"
Upper bound on the size of each rewritten chunk. Default 400, about a
paragraph or two: small chunks fit a 4,096-token context and cost little to
redo.
.TP
.BI \-\-parallel " N"
Chunks sent to the model at once, 1 to 16. Default 4. The server must run
them side by side to gain from it; for Ollama, set
.B OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=4
in its environment.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tuned
Use the plain model and the full voice prompt even if the voice has a
fine-tuned model.
.TP
.BI \-\-judge\-model " NAME"
Model that checks each changed sentence keeps its meaning. Default: the
base model of a fine-tuned voice, else
.BR \-\-model .
A different model costs a model switch per run on a GPU that holds only
one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-review
Keep each rewritten chunk whole, as checked by the chunk checks alone,
instead of reviewing it sentence by sentence.
.TP
.B \-\-every\-sentence
Rewrite every sentence, not only those that need work.
.TP
.B \-\-json\-diagnostics
Write a JSON run report to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
List every warning, one per chunk or paragraph. By default warnings are
summarized in at most three lines: chunks kept as written, sentences whose
original wording was kept, and style rules not fully met, each with a count
per reason.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE\fR, " \-o " FILE"
Write the result to
.I FILE
instead of standard output; it must not be an input file. A Markdown
input is written back as Markdown, with headings, code, tables and front
matter copied unchanged. Required when the input is a
.B .docx
file: its prose is rewritten while styles, headers, footers, tables,
images and character formatting are kept. Headings, captions, links,
fields, tracked changes and paragraphs that are not full sentences are
left as they are, and so is a title or cover page (a short first page ending in a
page or section break), unless
.B keep_title_page
is off in the settings file. The input file is never overwritten.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read settings from
.I FILE
instead of
.IR ~/.proselignrc .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore the settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Hide the progress line. By default, when standard error is a terminal,
an animated line shows how many chunks or paragraphs are done, the
elapsed time and an estimate of the time left, and a successful run
ends by printing the total time taken.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROSELIGN_BACKEND\fR, \fBPROSELIGN_ENDPOINT\fR, \fBPROSELIGN_MODEL
Defaults for the matching options.
.TP
.B PROSELIGN_HOME
Overrides the data directory.
.TP
.B PROSELIGN_CONFIG
Settings file to read instead of
.IR ~/.proselignrc .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Voices are stored in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/proselign/voices ,
default
.IR ~/.local/share/proselign/voices .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.proselignrc
INI settings for rewrites. Section
.B [rewrite]
sets
.BR voice ,
.BR strength ,
.BR format ,
.BR strict ,
.BR progress ,
.BR keep_title_page ,
.BR review ,
.BR every_sentence ,
.BR examples ,
.B candidates
and
.BR parallel ;
.B [backend]
sets
.BR backend ,
.BR endpoint ,
.BR model ,
.B judge_model
and
.BR offline ;
.B [style]
switches
.BR passive_voice ,
.BR en_dashes ,
.BR em_dashes ,
.BR exclamation_marks ,
.B semicolons
and
.B ai_artifact_filter
on or off, and sets
.B first_person
to
.BR voice ,
.B plural
(always we/us/our) or
.B singular
(I/me/my). Command-line options override environment variables, which
override this file. The file is refused if other users can write to it.
A commented sample is installed as
.IR /usr/share/doc/proselign/examples/proselignrc .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: bad arguments or unreadable input.
.TP
.B 3
Voice error: unknown, invalid or conflicting voice.
.TP
.B 4
Validation error: a rewrite failed fidelity checks under
.BR \-\-strict .
.TP
.B 5
Backend error: the inference endpoint is unreachable or replied badly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
proselign train \-\-voice Bryan ~/Documents/Writing/
cat draft.md | proselign \-\-voice Bryan > final.md
proselign \-\-voice Bryan \-\-strict \-\-strength 0.3 < memo.txt
proselign \-\-voice Bryan report.docx \-o report\-new.docx
proselign train \-\-voice BryanMail \-\-min\-words 150 Sent.mbox
proselign tune \-\-voice Bryan \-\-model qwen2.5:14b\-instruct
llama\-server \-m model.gguf \-\-port 8080 &
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://proselign.org
